 "steps": [
  {
   "caption": "Assume the whole implication is F. An implication is false only as T → F, so the hypothesis must be T and the conclusion F.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "n1",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "n2",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "e1",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "e2",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "The conclusion a → c is F, which forces a = T and c = F. These values are now fixed.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "n3",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "tone": "accent"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "e3",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "The hypothesis is a true conjunction, so both parts are T: a → b = T and b → c = T.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "n4",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "tone": "accent"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "e4",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "a is T and a → b is T, so b must be T (otherwise a → b would be T → F).",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "n5",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "tone": "accent"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "e5",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "b is T and b → c is T, so c must be T. But c was already forced to F.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "n6",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "tone": "accent"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "e6",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "A clash: no row can make the formula false, so it is a tautology. No branching was needed; every value was forced.",
